\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The level search on the two 17-terminal instances. Each point is a level tested by the cutting-plane evaluator, in the order of the binary search, plotted by its distance from the frontier value; filled markers are levels proved positive and hollow markers levels proved not positive. The distances shrink from above $2$ to the bracket of the final two levels; a level equal to the frontier value, and the last level of the refinement above it (at the distance $4.0\times 10^{-15}$ from the frontier value, below the floor), are both drawn at the floor $10^{-13}$.}}{29}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
