\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Lower bounds on the frontier constant by date and author. The instance values ($\tfrac  {16}{15}$, $1.28249$, $1.28260$, $1.17354$) are verified in this paper; the two family suprema, $\tfrac  98$ and $(299-41\sqrt  {41})/32$, are theorems of their sources [V], shown by the exact bracket of their value. General instances (blue, steps) and the planar series (red marks, one per source), with the line at $\tfrac  98$. The planar family point is the bracket of the supremum $(299-41\sqrt  {41})/32$ of the note of Protti and of the first preprint of Nikolenko; the point of $\tfrac  98$ is the planar family of Muffatti, plotted at the date printed on the note (24 July); the note was committed to its public repository on 23 July 2026 at 15:42 UTC, before the release of Protti (23 July 2026, 23:53 UTC); the planar record of $1.17353531974518$ is the highest planar value, and the 17-terminal refinement of $1.28260069$ is the highest general value. The upper bound $2$ for planar instances is outside the plotted range.}}{31}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ladder}{{7}{31}{Lower bounds on the frontier constant by date and author. The instance values ($\tfrac {16}{15}$, $1.28249$, $1.28260$, $1.17354$) are verified in this paper; the two family suprema, $\tfrac 98$ and $(299-41\sqrt {41})/32$, are theorems of their sources [V], shown by the exact bracket of their value. General instances (blue, steps) and the planar series (red marks, one per source), with the line at $\tfrac 98$. The planar family point is the bracket of the supremum $(299-41\sqrt {41})/32$ of the note of Protti and of the first preprint of Nikolenko; the point of $\tfrac 98$ is the planar family of Muffatti, plotted at the date printed on the note (24 July); the note was committed to its public repository on 23 July 2026 at 15:42 UTC, before the release of Protti (23 July 2026, 23:53 UTC); the planar record of $1.17353531974518$ is the highest planar value, and the 17-terminal refinement of $1.28260069$ is the highest general value. The upper bound $2$ for planar instances is outside the plotted range}{figure.7}{}}
